+aster-ath11k is a Rust port of parts of Linux's ath11k driver
+(drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k, Linux 6.18): the PCI register window and
+resets, the WLFW messages and their sequence, the HAL rings, the copy
+engines, HTC, WMI, HTT and the data path, and the station's command
+sequence, with the chips' tables generated from hw.c and ce.c. Linux licenses
+those files under the BSD-3-Clause-Clear licence, reproduced below. The
+port's own code is under the MPL-2.0, like the rest of this kernel.
+
+The MHI transport, the QRTR router and the QMI message encoding are this
+kernel's own implementations of those protocols (their register layouts,
+ring formats, packet headers and message types), written for interoperability
+without Linux's GPL-licensed code of them.
